      "answer": "**Step 1: Solve the equation**\nFirst, isolate the variable $z$ by adding 28 to both sides:\n$$6z = -196 + 28$$\n$$6z = -168$$\n\nNext, divide both sides by 6:\n$$z = \\frac{-168}{6}$$\n$$z = -28$$\n\n**Step 2: Verify by substitution**\nSubstitute $z = -28$ back into the original equation $6z + (-28) = -196$:\n$$6(-28) + (-28) = -196$$\n$$-168 - 28 = -196$$\n$$-196 = -196$$\n\nThe solution is correct.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n$$z = -28$$",
