      "answer": "```python\ndef unique_from_neg395_limit_4(items):\n    \"\"\"\n    Filter items to keep only those with values >= -395,\n    preserving the original order, and return at most 4 unique values.\n    \n    Edge-case semantics:\n    - If the list is empty, return an empty list.\n    - If the list contains only one item, return that item.\n    - If the list contains more than 4 items, return the first 4 unique values.\n    - If the list contains fewer than 4 items, return all of them.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items:\n        return []\n    \n    seen = set()\n    result = []\n    \n    for item in items:\n        if item >= -395 and item not in seen:\n            seen.add(item)\n            result.append(item)\n            if len(result) >= 4:\n                break\n    \n    return result\n```",
